From 4c4f9f7ad6483f2242a004277bc72428bbb99baa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kurt Kiefer <kkiefer@nvidia.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 12:53:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] nvgstplayer: force audioconvert when decoded format is a caps
 list

gst_structure_get_string() returns NULL when the "format" field is a
GValue list rather than a fixed string. This occurs with any libav
audio decoder whose underlying FFmpeg codec does not declare specific
output sample_fmts (e.g. avdec_amrnb, avdec_amrwb): gst-libav then
advertises a union of all possible GstAudioFormat values as a
GST_TYPE_LIST.

The NVGST_TARGET_TEGRA code path in create_audio_pipeline() guarded
the entire "needs conversion" decision inside if (format), so a NULL
format left NVGST_PLAY_FLAG_NATIVE_AUDIO set and skipped inserting
audioconvert into the audio bin. The downstream sink then received the
un-narrowed list caps, could not negotiate a fixed format, and returned
GST_FLOW_NOT_NEGOTIATED, surfacing as an "Internal data stream error"
from qtdemux.

A manually constructed pipeline (filesrc ! qtdemux ! avdec_amrnb !
audioconvert ! alsasink) plays correctly because audioconvert narrows
the list caps to a single negotiated format before alsasink sees them.
nvgstplayer bypasses GStreamer's standard playsink audio chain and
builds its own audio bin, so it does not benefit from playsink's
built-in audioconvert element.

On Ubuntu JetPack the bug went unnoticed because libasound2-plugins
routes the ALSA default PCM device through PulseAudio (pcm.!default
of type pulse). PulseAudio resolves list-type caps internally, so even
without audioconvert in the bin the pipeline negotiates successfully.
On OE4T there is no PulseAudio ALSA sink plugin and alsasink connects
directly to the hardware PCM, which requires a fixed format and fails
to negotiate the list.

Fix: treat a NULL format field (list/set type) the same as a
non-intersecting or float/unsigned format and force the audioconvert
path. Short-circuit evaluation of || ensures strstr() is never called
with a NULL pointer.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Kurt Kiefer <kkiefer@nvidia.com>
---
 nvgst_sample_apps/nvgstplayer-1.0/nvgstplayer.c | 8 +++-----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/nvgst_sample_apps/nvgstplayer-1.0/nvgstplayer.c b/nvgst_sample_apps/nvgstplayer-1.0/nvgstplayer.c
index 50aea77..23c6f5a 100644
--- a/nvgst_sample_apps/nvgstplayer-1.0/nvgstplayer.c
+++ b/nvgst_sample_apps/nvgstplayer-1.0/nvgstplayer.c
@@ -1974,11 +1974,9 @@ create_audio_pipeline (GstCaps * caps)
         channel_mask =
             gst_value_get_bitmask (gst_structure_get_value (str,
                 "channel-mask"));
-      if (format) {
-        if (!intersect || (strstr (format, "F")) || (strstr (format, "U"))
-            || (channel_mask != 0x3)) {
-          use_conv = app->input->attrs.flags &= ~NVGST_PLAY_FLAG_NATIVE_AUDIO;
-        }
+      if (!format || !intersect || (strstr (format, "F"))
+          || (strstr (format, "U")) || (channel_mask != 0x3)) {
+        use_conv = app->input->attrs.flags &= ~NVGST_PLAY_FLAG_NATIVE_AUDIO;
       }
 #else
       if (!intersect) {
